---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Explain original typed capture, suspension and cleanup observations without rerunning rustc

Usage: pse inspect compiler-facts [OPTIONS] <INVOCATION>

Arguments:
  <INVOCATION>

Options:
      --body <BODY>              Exact acquired body path; omitted selects all originally acquired bodies
  -C <checkout>
      --format <FORMAT>          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --max-bytes <MAX_BYTES>    Whole-body JSON payload budget; provenance is always retained [default: 16384]
      --fact-focus <FACT_FOCUS>  Select acquired detail before whole-body output budgeting; never acquires missing facts [default: all] [possible values: all, captures, suspension, cleanup]
      --fields <FIELDS>          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --budget <BUDGET>          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
  -h, --help                     Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Explain original typed capture, suspension and cleanup observations without rerunning rustc

Usage: pse inspect compiler-facts [OPTIONS] <INVOCATION>

Arguments:
  <INVOCATION>


Options:
      --body <BODY>
          Exact acquired body path; omitted selects all originally acquired bodies

  -C <checkout>


      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --max-bytes <MAX_BYTES>
          Whole-body JSON payload budget; provenance is always retained

          [default: 16384]

      --fact-focus <FACT_FOCUS>
          Select acquired detail before whole-body output budgeting; never acquires missing facts

          Possible values:
          - all:        Acquire all supported families within the selected owning body
          - captures:   Capture places, types, modes and source causes
          - suspension: Saved coroutine fields and their suspension variants
          - cleanup:    Analysis initialization and lowered normal/unwind cleanup

          [default: all]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
